          "new_text": "def filter_api_calls(\n    logp_with_result: np.ndarray,\n    logp_call_only: np.ndarray,\n    logp_no_call: np.ndarray,\n    tau_filter: float,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return an ordered keep mask and one finite margin per proposed call.\"\"\"\n    # Validate inputs\n    if isinstance(tau_filter, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must not be a boolean\")\n    if any(arr.ndim != 2 for arr in (logp_with_result, logp_call_only, logp_no_call)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrices must be 2D\")\n    if any(arr.size == 0 for arr in (logp_with_result, logp_call_only, logp_no_call)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrices must not be empty\")\n    if not (logp_with_result.shape == logp_call_only.shape == logp_no_call.shape):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrices must have the same shape\")\n    for arr in (logp_with_result, logp_call_only, logp_no_call):\n        if not np.all(np.isfinite(arr)):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input matrices must be finite\")\n        if np.any(arr > 0):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input matrices must be nonpositive\")\n    if not (np.isfinite(tau_filter) and tau_filter >= 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must be finite nonnegative\")\n    # Compute sums over horizon and margin\n    sum_with = np.sum(logp_with_result, axis=1)\n    sum_call = np.sum(logp_call_only, axis=1)\n    sum_no = np.sum(logp_no_call, axis=1)\n    margin = sum_with - np.maximum(sum_call, sum_no)\n    keep = margin >= tau_filter\n    return (keep, margin)"
